Track 2: "Did You Check the River Depth Before Leaving?"
- Story & Context: Sheltered beneath a blue plastic tarp during a flash thunderstorm along the Gyodong canal, guitarist Min-seo tracked her vocals while nursing bruised knuckles from pulling boat lines and shivering over a kerosene camping stove. She was wrestling with an acceptance letter from an overseas music conservatory while staring at her grandmother's rain-streaked radio antenna, realizing she could never bear to leave the estuary. Her voice breaks into a quiet, double-tracked falsetto over warbling Rhodes keys and an ascending tape riser that sounds like incoming surf: "I packed two clean shirts and my tuner, but my boots keep sinking into your bank." When the rain stopped, the damp cassette shell was labeled with the question Ok-ja had barked into the cabin right before hitting the red record switch.
